    "display_title": "fix(formation): read and write the unit store once a pass (Decision 144)",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "fix/unit-store-place-reads-once",
    "head_commit_message": "fix(formation): passes read units' places once instead of per unit\n\nStep 4's bench showed 4a's scattered place reads costing 22.6% on the\nRust engine (deaths, blows, the re-form's occupancy, units walking to\nplaces): each UnitPlace.of or rank was two store reads, and under Rust\neach read is a call into the field. UnitPlace.table fetches a squad's\nranks and columns once and UnitPlace.read reads a unit's place from\nthem. fighters(), ranged combat, SquadCompact (which now commits its\nranks once), the march's distances and pour targets, the re-form's\noccupancy and front-first order, SquadEdges, SquadGeometry, the trade,\nSquadRanks and the back-row counts fetch once a pass. No outcome\nchanges.\n\nTests: test_unit_place.gd checks a table reads each place as the store\nholds it on both backends (red on 4e's UnitPlace).\n\nWaived-by: Decision 142\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YWpV2AHWr3d2v4fKRki8G7",
